{
  "_comment": "Key -> file + mix. sound_events.json maps a gameplay MOMENT to a key here; nothing in .gd names a file. brand/SOUND_DESIGN.md is the design and the per-moment brief. Fields: volume (linear, on top of the player's master volume) | pool (how many of THIS sound may overlap; past it the oldest stops) | min_interval_ms (floor between two of the same sound — the anti-machine-gun) | pitch_jitter (SEMITONES either way, so a sound that fires constantly never repeats exactly) | pitch_ladder (semitone offsets a sound climbs while it keeps firing inside ladder_window_ms — the coin run) | max_distance + attenuation (positional sounds only) | loop is implied by use: attach_loop() loops whatever it is given.",
  "mix": {
    "_comment": "The mix, kept out of .gd because it is tuned by ear against the real files.",
    "max_voices": 12,
    "default_pool": 4,
    "default_max_distance": 420,
    "default_attenuation": 1.6,
    "music_volume": 1.0,
    "sfx_volume": 1.0,
    "ambience_volume": 1.0,
    "duck_db": -6.0,
    "duck_in_ms": 120,
    "duck_out_ms": 400,
    "music_crossfade_ms": 900,
    "music_fade_out_ms": 700
  },
