  "music": {
    "_comment": "One track per WORLD, named by theme rather than by level. The keys used to be level_01_music..level_05_music and the mapping was already strictly per theme -- every Emberwood level played level_01_music -- so the names described the wrong thing and levels 6-8 were correct only because the author repeated himself. data/themes/theme_<world>.json names the track; a level may still override it with its own `music`. `loop_offset` is seconds skipped when the track repeats: set it past the intro and the loop comes back to the groove instead of replaying the intro every time round, which is the most obvious 'this is a loop' tell there is. 0 until someone finds the musical point in a track.",
